BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 693.77 Tm (Every operator here starts from the same diagnosis: the money leaks through invoices nobody reads.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 678.55 Tm (ExpenseSavvy's host watched loan applicants obsess over revenue while their vendors sat on auto pay,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 663.32 Tm (with zero transparency into what the business down the street pays the same vendor for the same account) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 648.10 Tm ([2RDXap2GiBE @ 00:01:28]. brightfin hit the textbook version when pulling a new client's telecom invoices:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 632.87 Tm (the company had moved out of an office, emailed the carrier to shut the switch off, the switch never got shut) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 617.65 Tm (off, and finance kept paying because nobody told finance the office had closed; brightfin recouped roughly) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 602.42 Tm ($56,000 of that erroneous billing [lxObl7Zpr2A @ 00:03:06]. Auditel reports the same pattern on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 587.20 Tm (forward-savings work, where customers closed smaller satellite offices and neglected to cancel services,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 571.97 Tm (which the Auditel presenter says happens more than you might think [F00NVfaC6Tk @ 00:02:06].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 556.75 Tm (RadiusPoint goes further and says flatly that every client it was hired by faced waste and overspending in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 541.52 Tm (telecom, most were overpaying carriers, and none could trace their device inventory to a number, a location,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 526.30 Tm (and an end user ID [mFoRTIncoOI @ 00:03:17]. The consensus prerequisite is therefore inventory and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 511.07 Tm (visibility before negotiation: you cannot cut what you cannot map back to a live user or site.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 495.85 Tm (The commercial consensus is just as tight: the client pays nothing up front and the shop eats only from) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.62 Tm (savings it actually lands. Expense Consulting says it costs nothing to get started, the firm simply shares the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 465.40 Tm (savings it finds, claims it has found savings for 100% of its clients, and says those clients now average) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 450.17 Tm (savings in excess of 20% per year, with most saving within weeks [o2wyRpIYL0w @ 00:01:34]. Kirk Canol) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 434.95 Tm (of DCI Solutions pitches the identical no-risk structure, getting paid only after the client gets savings, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 419.72 Tm (backs it with hit rates: money recovered every time, savings 80% of the time in freight, telecom, and utilities,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 404.50 Tm (70% of the time in insurance, and half the time in office and warehouse supplies or refundable sales tax and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 389.27 Tm (unclaimed tax credits [meAxKn8Td5k @ 00:00:16]. Auditel frames telecom audits as contingency-based,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 374.05 Tm (meaning the client pays nothing if nothing is found, a no-risk, no-lose alternative to continuing to overpay) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 358.82 Tm ([YAHf-FXxBCM @ 00:01:52]. ExpenseSavvy runs the free analysis, charges nothing for the work, and takes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 343.60 Tm (a portion of savings only once the client starts saving [2RDXap2GiBE @ 00:03:51]. The second shared rule) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 328.37 Tm (is vendor neutrality: keep the incumbent, cut the price, a line DCI and Expense Consulting both repeat to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 313.15 Tm (clients.) Tj ET
